{
  "summary": "This experiment tested whether the image modality alone, encoded by ResNet-50 with a single profile and no aggregation or fusion, carries discriminative signal, yielding a validation accuracy of ~0.208 (F1: ~0.172). This is substantially below the RNA-only PCA(2000) single-profile baseline of ~0.485 (F1: ~0.464), suggesting that in this configuration the image modality provides limited discriminative information, though the comparison is confounded by the fundamentally different encoder types (pretrained CNN vs. linear PCA) and cannot definitively attribute the gap to image content versus encoder choice. It remains uncertain whether alternative image encoders, preprocessing, or fusion with the stronger RNA signal could recover useful information from the image modality, leaving open whether the multimodal branch of the design space warrants further search budget."
}

